  "notes": "mg90-c, the second motor, through second_motor_ident.py, identification.py executed again on motor-model's second_motor.py copies, every constant from mg90-c's own result files; every key defined as in mg90-b.json's notes. The pass reads capture-1's 5.0 and 7.4 V rungs (state A); its 3.7 V rungs are in bemf-coast's Ke reference but in no pass, and Ke is held out on the other two repeats at the same rungs. The ripple tach's gate drops the spins in tach_gate_dropped_spins (k, 7.4 V 60 % direction +1, seed difference 0.517 % over the 0.3 % limit) from Delta and V_b. pinned_c_negative_cuts lists the speed-torque cuts whose pinned read gives a negative c; the pass holding one is kept as it comes out, in c_a_s_per_v.pin and delta_f_ma_per_v. The meter runs are state C. r_board_ntc_move_pct's T_ref is mg90-c's stall pass, in sitting 2. Left out against mg90-b's file: error_angle_part_pct (rest-resistance runs no one-body split on mg90-c), error_vs_dmm_pct and hold_200ms_bias_pct (no ohms route; the hold-length refit is not run here), self_heat_bound_pct and self_heat_bound_runup_pct (no one-body map), ke_v_s_per_rad's four_coasts_rms_pct (the random draws are not run here)",
